====================================================================================
PART 4: THM-557 multi-cluster STRICTLY lowers the decorrelated cover (item 3)
====================================================================================
THM-557 (codex S61, EXACT Fraction integration): anchor 0 fixed, m=k-1 far runners partitioned
into coherent consecutive blocks; the SINGLE block [m] MAXIMIZES the shared-x decorrelated cover.
Closest split is always [m-1,1], with explicit POSITIVE split_gap. So any multi-cluster config's
decorrelated cover <= single-block D_m, and a SPLIT spends the split_gap as EXTRA margin.

